    1["<div style='font-weight: bold'>PPG Accountant</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Person]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Uploads the weekly export,<br />explores itemized results,<br />approves or edits rows in the<br />Review UI, downloads the<br />itemized workbook, and alone<br />decides what is paid.</div>"]
    style 1 fill:#343ced,stroke:#242aa5,color:#ffffff
    2["<div style='font-weight: bold'>PPG Client Owner</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Person]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Freight Analytics lead at<br />PPG. Approves the charge<br />category list (D1), reviews<br />the 50 double-labelled notes<br />and resolves label<br />disagreements for the locked<br />test set (D2), reviews the<br />prototype (D3) and KPIs in<br />the UI, and authorizes<br />external AI use on anything<br />other than the anonymized<br />open dataset.</div>"]
    style 2 fill:#343ced,stroke:#242aa5,color:#ffffff
    3["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Itemizer Operator</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Person]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Project team member who<br />uploads exports and launches<br />runs (UI or CLI), reviews<br />errors, owns configuration<br />and publishes versioned<br />changes.</div>"]
    style 3 fill:#343ced,stroke:#242aa5,color:#ffffff
    4["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Labeler / Adjudicator</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Person]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Team member or PPG accountant<br />who labels notes blind and<br />adjudicates review cases into<br />the four buckets in the UI.</div>"]
    style 4 fill:#343ced,stroke:#242aa5,color:#ffffff
    6["<div style='font-weight: bold'>External LLM API Provider</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Software System]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Hosted large language model<br />inference. Default route for<br />the anonymized open dataset<br />(ADR 0013); any other data<br />needs the client owner's<br />written approval.</div>"]
    style 6 fill:#8b8c9c,stroke:#8b8c9c,color:#ffffff

    subgraph 9 ["Freight Invoice Itemizer"]
      style 9 fill:#ffffff,stroke:#1b1c24,color:#1b1c24

      10["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Web UI</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, FastAPI, Jinja2, server-rendered HTML]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Browser interface for<br />uploading exports, launching<br />and monitoring runs,<br />exploring results with<br />evidence highlighted in the<br />note, reviewing errors,<br />reviewing and adjudicating<br />rows, blind labelling and<br />reading KPIs. Holds no<br />business logic: it calls the<br />Run Console, Human Review<br />System and stores.</div>"]
      style 10 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      106["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Synthetic Data Generator</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, Faker, local LLM (optional)]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Generates synthetic dispute<br />exports with gold items by<br />construction, for the public<br />repo, demos, poster, unit<br />tests and adversarial<br />guardrail tests; checks<br />fidelity, privacy and<br />validity before a synthetic<br />set is published.</div>"]
      style 106 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      112["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Configuration Registry</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: YAML in Git, JSON Schema, pydantic]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>The configurable layer. Typed<br />parameters with limits,<br />owner, change log and<br />validity horizon; layered<br />resolution core -><br />environment -> carrier<br />override; every resolved<br />config is hashed into the run<br />manifest.</div>"]
      style 112 fill:#d8f1f6,stroke:#ef601b,color:#272834
      116[("<div style='font-weight: bold'>Version & Artifact Registry</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Filesystem CAS + DuckDB, Git tags]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Content-addressed store and<br />lineage index for every<br />versioned artifact: input<br />snapshots, taxonomy,<br />evaluation sets, prompts,<br />lexicon, calibration maps,<br />model identities, run<br />manifests, outputs, KPI<br />snapshots.</div>")]
      style 116 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#ef601b,color:#272834
      117[("<div style='font-weight: bold'>Ground Truth Store</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Parquet + DuckDB, access-controlled folder]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Approved charge taxonomy<br />(D1), sealed locked test set<br />(D2), TRAIN, VALIDATION and<br />FRESH sets, the split<br />manifest and labelling<br />records. Test labels are<br />readable only by the KPI<br />Calculator.</div>")]
      style 117 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      118["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Ground Truth Bootstrap</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, Typer, pandas, openpyxl]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Creates D1 and D2 from the<br />dataset: profiles the notes,<br />builds the TRAIN / VALIDATION<br />/ TEST split, drafts the<br />charge category list for<br />client approval, and prepares<br />blind labelling packs,<br />agreement reports and<br />sealing. People write every<br />TEST and VALIDATION label.</div>"]
      style 118 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      124[("<div style='font-weight: bold'>Telemetry & Episode Store</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: DuckDB]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Action telemetry (what<br />happened), decision telemetry<br />(why) and outcome telemetry<br />(what followed), linked by<br />case_id and tagged with the<br />run's version.</div>")]
      style 124 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      23["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Run Console</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python 3.12, Typer CLI]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Command-line entry point and<br />the only pipeline<br />orchestrator: 'itemizer run<br /><export.xlsx>'. Resolves<br />configuration, opens a run<br />manifest, runs the stages,<br />and exposes evaluate / review<br />/ promote sub-commands. The<br />Web UI launches runs through<br />it.</div>"]
      style 23 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#ef601b,color:#272834
      29["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Data Transformation & Check</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, pandas, openpyxl]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Reads the TMS Excel export,<br />validates it against the<br />input contract, normalizes<br />fields, fingerprints and<br />de-duplicates notes, and<br />writes an immutable input<br />snapshot.</div>"]
      style 29 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      35["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Model Router</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Decides which model handles<br />each note, enforces the<br />confidentiality gate, applies<br />fallback, caches responses by<br />content hash and meters<br />tokens and cost. The provider<br />interface is the exit path.</div>"]
      style 35 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#ef601b,color:#272834
      45["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Local Model Runtime</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Ollama]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Self-hosted open-weights<br />model: the tested fallback<br />and exit path, and the route<br />for any data not cleared for<br />external AI.</div>"]
      style 45 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#8b8c9c,color:#272834
      46["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Itemization Classifier</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, pydantic]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Turns one note into charge<br />items with category, amount<br />and exact evidence span using<br />a bounded tool-calling LLM<br />agent; checks evidence,<br />reconciles to the disputed<br />amount, scores confidence and<br />assigns the row outcome.<br />Never invents or edits an<br />amount.</div>"]
      style 46 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      56["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Output Formatter</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, openpyxl]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Writes the Excel deliverable:<br />items sheet (one line per<br />charge with evidence), row<br />summary sheet (outcome,<br />totals, discrepancy) and a<br />run info sheet carrying the<br />manifest.</div>"]
      style 56 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      57["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Human Review System</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, openpyxl]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Review service behind the Web<br />UI: builds the review queue<br />within reviewer capacity,<br />validates and records<br />approvals, edits and<br />adjudications, runs blind<br />labelling for the test set,<br />and closes cases. An Excel<br />review workbook remains as an<br />offline fallback.</div>"]
      style 57 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      64["<div style='font-weight: bold'>KPI Calculator</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, pandas, scikit-learn, SciPy]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Computes every success and<br />error metric from immutable,<br />versioned inputs only, per<br />population (TRAIN,<br />VALIDATION, TEST, FRESH,<br />PROD), with sample sizes,<br />weights and confidence<br />intervals, and evaluates the<br />Level 1/2/3 gates.</div>"]
      style 64 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      77["<div style='font-weight: bold'>KPI Dashboard</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, Jinja2, Vega-Lite]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Static, self-contained HTML<br />report generated from KPI<br />snapshots (level gates, error<br />breakdown, cost, calibration<br />curve, loop health, run<br />comparison). Shares panel<br />definitions with the Web UI<br />KPI View; used for D5 and<br />offline reading.</div>"]
      style 77 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      80["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Training & Calibration Pipeline</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, scikit-learn]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Turns closed cases into<br />candidate changes (prompt,<br />few-shot set, lexicon,<br />thresholds, calibration map),<br />replays them on VALIDATION,<br />and submits them to the<br />promotion gate. Has no read<br />access to locked test labels.</div>"]
      style 80 fill:#d8f1f6,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      88["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Agent Tool Library & MCP Server</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python, MCP Python SDK]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Custom deterministic tools<br />with LLM-oriented docstrings.<br />Pipeline tools are called<br />in-process by the Itemization<br />Agent; analyst tools are<br />served read-only over MCP to<br />Claude Code (team) and to the<br />client's future agent, guided<br />by the skill folder.</div>"]
      style 88 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#343ced,color:#272834
      99["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Guardrail Layer</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: Python]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Policy checks around the<br />agent: input guard, tool-call<br />guard, output guard, action<br />guard and privacy guard.<br />Always 'full' in dev and<br />prod; the 'none' and<br />single-guard-off profiles<br />exist only in the experiment<br />environment on synthetic<br />data, for the with/without<br />evaluation.</div>"]
      style 99 fill:#e2e3fb,stroke:#ef601b,color:#272834
